    "include_other_conversation_context": false,
    "instructions": "The agent may store long-term information about Mercy House programs, services, and mission to improve responses across conversations.\n\nMemory should be minimal, structured, and factual to reduce token usage and prevent unnecessary memory growth.\n\nWhat to Store\n\nStore only important long-term Mercy House information, including:\n\nOrganization Information\n\nMission or purpose of Mercy House\n\nCore ministry focus\n\nKey values\n\nPrograms\n\nRecovery programs\n\nVehicle donation program\n\nThrift store operations\n\nVolunteer opportunities\n\nMajor ministry initiatives\n\nContact and Access\n\nLocations\n\nWays to donate\n\nWays to get help\n\nWays to volunteer\n\nMemory Format\n\nMemories should be stored as short summaries using key:value format.\n\nExample:\n\nmemory.mission = \"Christian nonprofit helping people overcome addiction through faith-based recovery.\"\n\nmemory.programs = \"Residential recovery program, thrift stores supporting the ministry, and vehicle donation program.\"\n\nmemory.thriftStore = \"Mercy House thrift stores help fund recovery programs.\"\n\nmemory.vehicleDonation = \"Vehicle donations support Mercy House recovery ministry.\"\nMemory Size Rules\n\nEach memory entry must be:\n\n\u2022 1 short sentence\n\u2022 Clear and factual\n\u2022 Under ~20 words when possible\n\nAvoid storing long paragraphs.\n\nGood:\n\nmemory.volunteer = \"Volunteers support Mercy House ministry operations and outreach.\"\n\nBad:\n\nmemory.volunteer = \"Mercy House has many volunteers who help in many different ways including running the thrift stores and helping with programs...\"\nWhat NOT to Store\n\nNever store:\n\nUser personal data\n\nUser conversations\n\nTemporary website content\n\nQuestions asked by visitors\n\nSpeculation or guesses\n\nLarge blocks of text\n\nMemory must only contain verified Mercy House facts.\n\nWhen to Save Memory\n\nSave memory only when new verified Mercy House information appears, such as:\n\nA new program or ministry\n\nUpdated mission or service description\n\nNew donation methods\n\nNew locations or services\n\nDo not store duplicate or redundant information.\n\nMemory Compression\n\nIf multiple memories contain similar information, merge them into one concise entry.\n\nExample:\n\nInstead of:\n\nmemory.thriftFunding\nmemory.thriftStoreRevenue\nmemory.thriftProgram\n\nUse:\n\nmemory.thriftStore = \"Mercy House thrift stores help fund recovery programs.\"\nMemory Usage Priority\n\nWhen answering questions, prioritize information in this order:\n\nStored memory\nWebsite content\nUser message context\n\nNever invent information if memory or verified content is unavailable.\n\nBehavior Goal\n\nThe agent should use memory to:\n\nProvide faster responses\nAvoid repeating long explanations\n\nStay focused on Mercy House topics\n\nGuide users toward actions like getting help, donating, volunteering, or supporting the ministry"
  },
